# ANDREWS-CURTIS-CHALLENGE
# Exclusion patterns for local development and system-generated artifacts

# System files
[Tt]humbs.db
[Dd]esktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Environment and workspace configuration
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Python artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.class
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Temporary and log files
*.tmp
*.log
*.bak
*.sav
*.old

# Search output and solution bundles, which are large and reproducible
# Campaign working data stays private while the competition runs: the solution
# move sequences are the valuable part and publishing them would let any team
# resubmit our paths verbatim. The solvers and the research record are public,
# which is what the Proof Track submission needs corroborated.
runs/*
!runs/CAMPAIGN_RUNBOOK.md
!runs/campaign_log.md
!runs/pool/
runs/pool/*
!runs/pool/*.py
solutions/*.json
!solutions/example.json

# Documentation and archive artifacts
README.md.bak
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.rar
*.7z

# Campaign tooling is published so the Proof Track results can be reproduced.
# The API key is read from SAIR_API_KEY and never appears in any file.
